dressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUKI, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HONMURA SHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAMIMURA TAKEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIDA KIYONORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASAKI KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANII TADAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUZUKI SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YABUKI MASAKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HONMURA, SHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMIMURA, TAKEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIDA, KIYONORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANII, TADAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUZUKI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUKI, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for crushing a used lithium ion cell safely with high efficiency characterized by comprising a case crushing/separating step of separating a plastic case protecting a sealed cell body safely and reliably to the outside of the system, and separately recovering valuable substances such as lithium cobaltate which is a lithium-transition metal complex oxide, aluminum, and copper by repeatedly vibrating or pressing the cell cooled at -50  DEG C or less by utilizing materials having a rigidity and a specific gravity both higher than those of plastic material of the plastic case so as to separate the cell into the sealed cell body and the plastic case, a heating separating step of heating the separated cell body at 200  DEG C or more in a non-oxidizing atmosphere to separate mainly organic substances, and one or more separating steps of removing noise substances from the chips produced in the cell crushing step in order so as to obtain objective useful substances.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé sûr et efficace de déchiquetage des piles à ions lithium comportant: les étapes suivantes: écrasement/séparation de l'étui plastique protégeant sûrement et fiablement le corps de pile de l'extérieur; séparation/récupération des substances précieuses telles que le lithium cobaltate, oxyde complexe de lithium et d'un métal de transition, l'aluminium, et le cuivre, sous l'effet de vibrations et de compressions répétées, ou de compressions à -50  DEG C ou moins en utilisant des matériaux d'une rigidité et d'un poids spécifique dépassant ceux formant l'enveloppe afin de séparer l'étui du corps; chauffage/séparation du corps à 200  DEG C ou plus dans une atmosphère non oxydante pour séparer les substances principalement organique; et une ou plusieurs étapes d'élimination des substances parasites produites lors du déchiquetage pour obtenir des substances directement utilisables.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>